## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical DP reasoning: variable step costs require deriving both a memoized and a tabular solution, handle unreachable states, and discuss trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Top-down DP with memoization
- Bottom-up DP (tabulation)
- Handling unreachable states with Infinity
- Time/space complexity: O(n|S|) time, O(n) space

## Code Example

```javascript
function minCostTopDown(n, steps, memo=new Map()){
  if(n===0) return 0
  if(n<0) return Infinity
  if(memo.has(n)) return memo.get(n)
  let best = Infinity
  for(let s of steps){
    const c = s + minCostTopDown(n-s, steps, memo)
    if(c < best) best = c
  }
  memo.set(n, best)
  return best
}

function minCostBottomUp(n, steps){
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY
  const dp = Array(n+1).fill(INF)
  dp[0] = 0
  for(let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    for(let s of steps){
      if(i>=s && dp[i-s] !== INF){
        dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], s + dp[i-s])
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n] === INF ? -1 : dp[n]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt if costs were a non-linear function cost(s) instead of s? 
- How would you extend to count the number of ways to reach n with min cost, not just the cost itself?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP on strings, demonstrating memoization vs tabulation and optimization tricks.

## Key Concepts
- Pattern matching with Trie to prune dictionary checks
- Top-down vs bottom-up DP on string indices
- Handling empty inputs and modulo arithmetic

## Code Example
```javascript
function countWays(s, dict){
  const trie = buildTrie(dict);
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  dp[n] = 1;
  for(let i = n-1; i >= 0; --i){
    let node = trie;
    for(let j = i; j < n; j++){
      const c = s[j];
      if(!node.next[c]) break;
      node = node.next[c];
      if(node.end) dp[i] += dp[j+1];
    }
  }
  return dp[0];
}
function buildTrie(words){
  const root = {next:{}, end:false};
  for(const w of words){
    let node = root;
    for(const ch of w){
      if(!node.next[ch]) node.next[ch] = {next:{}, end:false};
      node = node.next[ch];
    }
    node.end = true;
  }
  return root;
}
```

